                    briefing_text_r4:       `The split Board votes today — three community-elected trustees, four appointed — and you must win approval <strong>and</strong> hold legitimacy; they cannot be traded. Win 4–3 on pure content while the three community trustees vote against, and the forum reads “imposed from above” within the hour. This morning a coalition of 600 editors threatens a 30-day editing freeze unless the AI clause is withdrawn — that is 0.25% of your editors setting strategy by ultimatum. <em>Capitulate instantly and every future decision is hostage; ignore them and you lose the room.</em> Is there a conditional version that holds the plan AND the relationship? Commit the governance that carries it to 2031, then close the loop with the community.`,

